title:    The route nobody wrote
subtitle: The hub learned 10.30.0.0/24 twice — once per tunnel — and it appears in no route resource
width:    960
---
$ gcloud compute routers get-status hub-router --region us-central1

bgpPeerStatus:
  name                 state         numLearnedRoutes  peerIpAddress
  hub-peer-t0          Established   1                 169.254.0.2
  hub-peer-t1          Established   1                 169.254.1.2

bestRoutes:
  destRange       nextHopIp       priority
  10.30.0.0/24    169.254.0.2     100
  10.30.0.0/24    169.254.1.2     100

$ grep -rn "10.30.0.0/24" terraform/*.tf

terraform/variables.tf:15:  default = "10.30.0.0/24"

# ONE match, and it is a SUBNET definition on the branch side. There is no
# google_compute_route anywhere in this week, and no static route was typed
# on either end.
#
# The hub knows how to reach the branch because the two Cloud Routers opened
# BGP sessions over the tunnels and told each other what they could reach.
# Two sessions, two advertisements, two entries at equal priority - so traffic
# can use either, and losing one leaves the other.
#
# 169.254.x.x are the link-local /30s the BGP sessions run over. No workload
# ever uses them; they exist so the routers have somewhere to talk.
